                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>Through classroom instruction on the fundamentals and clinical aspects of obstetrics and gynecology outlined in the syllabus, students will master the basic knowledge and theoretical principles regarding the etiology, clinical characteristics, and diagnostic and therapeutic principles of common and frequently occurring diseases in obstetrics and gynecology. They will also gain an understanding of relevant new developments in the field. This course lays the theoretical and practical foundation for medical students to pursue future careers in obstetrics and gynecology-related oral health work.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
